@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# Internal mouse-dispatch validity
+
+This is an implementation contract, not the public component API. `Component.handleMouse` still returns `TuiMouseEventResult` (`handled`, `capture`, `focus`, `render`). Raw dispatch targets and helpers are internal and are not exported by the package root.
+
+## Provenance
+
+`TuiMouseDispatchTarget.validity` separates:
+
+- `path`: inherited delegation/ownership/geometry guards. Each guard has a `scope`, a `subject`, and `isValid`. The identity pair `(scope, subject)` names one actual ownership/geometry generation and the specific registration it protects. Fresh callbacks for the same pair must describe that same lifetime. Component identity, equal rectangles, callback identity, and callback text do not establish lifetime identity.
+- `current`: the current target's replaceable predicate. A new explicit predicate supersedes the previous current constraint. A same-target recapture with `current: undefined` (including a plain result without metadata) retains the last current constraint; an explicit `current: () => true` replaces it with an unconstrained current predicate. A valid handoff supersedes the outgoing current constraint, but never the inherited path.
+
+Fullscreen retains the original press validity separately. Its inherited path is retained even if the press did not request capture. Original press ownership remains an invariant throughout subsequent handoffs.
+
+`withMouseDispatchValidity` derives the combined `isValid` compatibility predicate from this metadata. `withMouseDispatchGuard` extends the inherited path without obscuring the current predicate. Dispatch copies forwarded result metadata before composing guards, so reusing a producer-owned structured response cannot accumulate path history. Existing consumers, including MainScreenMouse, continue reading the combined predicate; their routing policy is unchanged.
+
+An internal target supplying `isValid` without explicit provenance is malformed. Dispatch and composition fail with `Mouse dispatch invariant: isValid requires explicit validity provenance`. There is no opaque-producer escape hatch, current-only reinterpretation, unbounded legacy history, or transfer-count cap. Plain public handler results require no new fields.
+
+## Built-in identities
+
+- Container/Box: the committed mouse-layout token supplies the geometry generation; a per-child-slot lifetime token supplies the subject, including distinct occurrences of the same component; removal/clear revokes that lifetime. Removing or clearing a child revokes its lifetime, even if the same component object is re-added with identical output. Distinct children sharing a container layout have distinct subjects.
+- Overlays: a rendered overlay-layout entry supplies the geometry generation; its visibility lifetime supplies the subject. Hide/show revokes the previous visibility lifetime.
+- Structural fullscreen and bounded layouts: LayoutBox records the actual structural registration. MouseLayoutScopes reconciles registrations through their owning ancestry and retains scope identities only while the same registration has unchanged allocated bounds, clipping, line offset and logical height. Changed or removed scopes are revoked, not revived by a later matching frame. Temporary bounded allocation entries retain their owner's registration rather than inventing a new registration each render. BoundedVStack additionally retains its existing whole-layout token guard: a structural/logical-height change to another bounded child cancels the path even when the target rectangle is unchanged. Scope predicates retain compact registration paths and scalar geometry, not historical LayoutBox trees; historical sibling trees must remain collectible.
+
+These registries are instance-owned, not global. Mutation through ownership methods (`removeChild`, `clear`, overlay hide/show and layout-root replacement) revokes ownership independently of final component/rectangle equality. Render commits additionally revoke moved, resized, clipped, or removed structural paths. Direct remove-and-reinsert mutations that leave no observable state and bypass ownership methods cannot supply a lifetime notification; this contract does not manufacture one from equal final arrays.
+
+## Capture lifecycle and cost
+
+Fullscreen stores inherited guards by `(scope, subject)`, not by fresh callback identity. Repeated handoffs among unchanged finite scopes therefore retain at most those scopes. Validation cost depends on the retained scopes, not pointer-report count. Current target metadata is replaced without recursive validator chains.
+
+Validate before and after mouse callbacks, after focus setters before installing new capture metadata, and on committed frames. After focus, validate both the old capture/original press/inherited path and the incoming target. An invalid incoming request cancels the gesture; it must not leave a previous permissive capture active. Lifecycle generation checks prevent stopped/restarted or reentrant callbacks from restoring an obsolete gesture.
+
+Once invalidated, the gesture remains canceled until it ends. Redraw intent is independent: a canceled callback can still request repaint. Neither rendering nor historical-guard deduplication authorizes reviving a removed registration.
